# NodeJS REST API自定义404响应：替换默认Cannot Get提示
created: undefined, last updated: 2026-06-11, [Read more](https://www.volcengine.com/article/431169)

Express processes middleware and routes in the exact order you define them.
To catch all undefined routes, you just need to add a **catch-all middleware at the very end** of your route definitions (after all your API endpoints like `/api/domains.json`).
Here's the snippet you need to add:
```
// Catch all undefined routes and return custom 404 JSON
app.use((req, res) => {
res.status(404).json({ code: 404, message: "Not found" });
});
...
By placing this middleware last, Express will only trigger it if none of your defined routes match the incoming request.
This completely replaces the default "Cannot GET /ROUTE" message with your clean, custom JSON response.
